      "content": "that's a good direction. let's lean into that even more. can you finish that last thought and then add a closing part that really drives home the idea that there is no 'neutral' ground? i want to argue that by not voting, you are actually making a choice to support the status quo and the people currently in power. frame it so that silence or inaction isn't just being 'undecided,' it's actively helping the very people people complain about.",
